        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe consolidation itself is largely well-shaped and idiomatic for this codebase: folding `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` into one `OwnerMemberId` \"single source of truth\" class mirrors the existing `OwnerCustomerCode` pattern, the Luhn helper correctly moves in from the now-deleted `OwnerCheckDigit` (a dedicated class was only justified while the check digit was a standalone field), and `AssignOwnerMemberId`, `OwnerPrimaryIdentifier`, the audit record, and the schema/OpenAI changes all read cleanly. But there's a coherence problem around the fiscal-year label:\n\n**The `FY` label format is now duplicated, and `OwnerFiscalYear`'s javadoc contradicts the actual code path.**\n\n- `OwnerMemberId.fiscalYearLabel` independently reconstructs the label with a hardcoded `\"FY\" + memberId.substring(...)`. The literal `FY` prefix convention also lives in `OwnerFiscalYear.label`. The format of a fiscal-year label is now defined in two classes, so a change to that convention (e.g. `FY` \u2192 `FY-`) must be made in both or they drift.\n- Worse, the diff's own updated `OwnerFiscalYear` javadoc now claims: *\"the `memberId`'s `FY` segment (from which the read-time `fiscalYear` field is read back) ... resolves through this class so they cannot drift apart.\"* That is no longer true \u2014 the read-back does **not** resolve through `OwnerFiscalYear`; it is done entirely inside `OwnerMemberId.fiscalYearLabel` with its own `FY` literal. The comment asserts a single-source-of-truth guarantee the code does not provide.\n\nSuggested fix: have the label-formatting live in one place. Either `OwnerMemberId.fiscalYearLabel` should return the raw two-digit segment and let `OwnerFiscalYear` own the `FY` prefix (e.g. add an `OwnerFiscalYear.label(String yy)` / `labelFromDigits` that the memberId read-back and the date-based path both call), or drop the inaccurate \"resolves through this class\" claim from `OwnerFiscalYear`'s javadoc and instead state plainly that the label prefix is reproduced in `OwnerMemberId`. The first option is preferable \u2014 it keeps the fiscal-year label format in a single unit and makes the `OwnerFiscalYear` javadoc honest.\n\nMinor: `AssignOwnerMemberId`/`OwnerMemberId.deduplicate` still de-duplicates by appending `-<n>`, which introduces a `-` into an id documented (OpenAPI, class javadoc) as having \"no separators.\" Not a structural fault of this diff per se (it inherits the prior dedup approach), but on a now-separatorless format it's worth a note so the separator convention stays coherent."
